  {
   "title": "me gustaría = I would like",
   "body": "Start with the verb: it would please (gustaría), then who it pleases (nos). The thing liked here is 'to eat', which is singular, so it's gustaría, not gustarían.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I'd like to eat now.",
     "es": "Me gustaría comer ahora."
    },
    {
     "en": "We'd like to eat now.",
     "es": "Nos gustaría comer ahora."
    },
    {
     "en": "I'd like to see you.",
     "es": "Me gustaría verte."
    }
   ],
   "t": 185.8
  },
  {
   "title": "podría = could",
   "body": "Common verbs get worn down: podería lost its e and became podría.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "I / he could",
     "es": "podría"
    },
    {
     "en": "they / you / we could",
     "es": "podrían / podrías / podríamos"
    }
   ],
   "t": 277.2
  },
  {
   "title": "Polite requests with podrías",
   "body": "Mi casa = my house. Decir = to say / tell.",
   "examples": [
    {
     "en": "Could you come to my house?",
     "es": "¿Podrías venir a mi casa?"
